l\", \"identifier\": {\"@type\": \"PropertyValue\", \"propertyID\": \"GSS code\", \"value\": \"E08000038\"}, \"areaServed\": \"Yorkshire and the Humber\", \"memberOf\": [{\"@type\": \"GovernmentOrganization\", \"name\": \"South Yorkshire Mayoral Combined Authority\", \"url\": \"https://wherecouncilsstand.com/councils/E47000002\"}]}}</script>\n  </head><body><main id=\"main\"><div id=\"app\"><p class=\"meta\"><a href=\"/councils\">Councils</a> · Metropolitan borough council · Yorkshire and the Humber</p><h1>Barnsley Metropolitan Borough Council</h1><p>Part of: <a href=\"/councils/E47000002\">South Yorkshire Mayoral Combined Authority</a>.</p><p>Full council and cabinet meetings from February 2025 to February 2025, read from the council's <a href=\"https://barnsleymbc.moderngov.co.uk\">own record</a>.</p><ul><li>In overall control: Labour, as listed on 26 February 2025</li><li>1 meeting: 1 full council, 0 cabinet</li><li>1 named vote recorded in the minutes</li></ul><h2>On Where Landlords Stand</h2><ul><li><a href=\"https://wherelandlordsstand.com/landlords/barnsley-metropolitan-borough-council/\">Barnsley Metropolitan Borough Council as a landlord</a></li><li><a href=\"https://wherelandlordsstand.com/areas/barnsley/\">The 18 social landlords with homes in Barnsley</a></li></ul><h2>Members by party</h2><p>The 3 councillors listed at the full council meeting of 26 February 2025, with their party as the council recorded it.</p><ul><li>Labour: 2</li><li>Liberal Democrats: 1</li></ul><h2>Party in overall control</h2><ul><li>From February 2025: Labour</li></ul><h2>Named votes (1)</h2><ol><li><a href=\"/votes/E08000038:1:10:0\">Notice of Motion - Weekly Bin Collections</a>: Full council, 26 February 2025, a named vote on the motion, lost. For 1, Against 2, Abstained 0.</li></ol><h2>Latest meetings</h2><ul><li>26 February 2025: <a href=\"u\">Full Council</a></li></ul><h2>Statements in their own words</h2><article class=\"statement\"><h3>Statement from Steve Houghton, 14 November 2026</h3><p>Councillor, Barnsley Metropolitan Borough Council</p><p>About: <a href=\"/votes/E08000038:1:10:0\">Notice of Motion - Weekly Bin Collections, 26 February 2025</a></p><p>I voted against this motion because the council had already agreed a review of collections, and the minutes of that meeting set it out.</p><p><a href=\"https://barnsley.moderngov.co.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?MId=1\">The record they point to</a></p><p><em>In their own words. Not checked or endorsed by Where Councils Stand.</em></p></article></div></main></body></html>",
