s/E08000038\"}, {\"@type\": \"Event\", \"name\": \"Barnsley Metropolitan Borough Council: Full council, 26 February 2025\", \"startDate\": \"2025-02-26\", \"url\": \"https://example/E08000038/10\"}]}</script>\n  </head><body><main id=\"main\"><div id=\"app\"><p class=\"meta\"><a href=\"/councils\">Councils</a> · <a href=\"/councils/E08000038\">Barnsley Metropolitan Borough Council</a></p><h1>Notice of Motion - Weekly Bin Collections</h1><p>Full council, 26 February 2025: a named vote on the motion, lost.</p><p>For 1, Against 2, Abstained 0.</p><p>Party in overall control of the council on the date: Labour. Each councillor's party is the one the council recorded for them at the time.</p><h2>For (1)</h2><ul><li>Hannah Kitching (Liberal Democrats)</li></ul><h2>Against (2)</h2><ul><li>Robin Franklin (Labour)</li><li>Sir Steve Houghton (Labour)</li></ul><h2>From the minutes</h2><blockquote><p>Upon being put to the vote the motion was lost.</p></blockquote><p><a href=\"https://example/E08000038/10\">The item in the council&#x27;s own minutes</a>. Names are matched to the councillors listed at the meeting. The names of people who aren't councillors are removed.</p><article class=\"statement\"><h2>Statement from Steve Houghton, 14 November 2026</h2><p>Councillor, Barnsley Metropolitan Borough Council</p><p>I voted against this motion because the council had already agreed a review of collections, and the minutes of that meeting set it out.</p><p><a href=\"https://barnsley.moderngov.co.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?MId=1\">The record they point to</a></p><p><em>In their own words. Not checked or endorsed by Where Councils Stand.</em></p></article></div></main></body></html>",
